  "question": {
    "text": "Let the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;contain the line of intersection of two planes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"bold-italic\">r</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>. If the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mn>13</mn><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
